    "8:11–21 — Pharisees come forth and begin to question him, seeking of him a sign from heaven, tempting him. He sighs deeply in his spirit: Why doth this generation seek after a sign? verily I say unto you, There shall no sign be given unto this generation. He leaves them, entering into the ship again. The disciples had forgotten to take bread; they had no more than one loaf. He charged them, Take heed, beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, and of the leaven of Herod. They reason, It is because we have no bread. He: Why reason ye, because ye have no bread? perceive ye not yet, neither understand? have ye your heart yet hardened? Having eyes, see ye not? Having ears, hear ye not? and do ye not remember? When I brake the five loaves among five thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up? Twelve. And when the seven among four thousand, how many baskets? Seven. How is it that ye do not understand?",
